WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.308
"Are Plant Sterols Effective for Lowering Cholesterol?"

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.080
The Dietary Guidelines cite
the National Academies

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.200
in recommending that
"dietary cholesterol consumption

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.080
be as low as possible."

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.000
While eggs are
the most concentrated source

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.680
of cholesterol gram-for-gram,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.960
the greatest contribution
in the American diet is meat,

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.800
including poultry and fish.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.160
But even if
our cholesterol intake is zero,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.840
if you remember
from my earlier video,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.240
our liver dumps
excess cholesterol

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.200
into our digestive tract
through the bile,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.400
expecting there to be
about a hundred grams of fiber

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.640
in there every day
to trap it and flush it

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.720
out of the body,

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.520
but when people are getting
five to ten times less fiber

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.640
than nature intended,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.880
much of that cholesterol
gets reabsorbed

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.600
and can circulate
back through our system.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.520
That's why
one of the components

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.560
of the cholesterol-lowering
Portfolio Diet

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.000
are foods like oatmeal

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.200
that are high in sticky fiber
that traps cholesterol,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.720
but the diet also includes
phytosterols, plant sterols.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.680
This is what cholesterol
looks like.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.720
This is what one
of the phytosterols looks like.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.240
It's almost identical.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.280
And the receptor here
in the lining of our intestine

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.280
can't tell the difference;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.760
so, the phytosterols
compete with cholesterol

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.240
to squeeze in
through this receptor.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.560
So, if there's a lot
of phytosterols in the gut,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.680
some of the cholesterol
can't get in or back in

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:36.080
and ends up in the toilet
instead of our bloodstream.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.600
Here's fecal cholesterol
excretion in people

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.760
eating different amounts
of phytosterols.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.160
The black is the amount
of dietary cholesterol

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.160
that's being pooped out,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.920
and the white is the amount
of cholesterol

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.840
that our liver dumps
into our intestine

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.280
through the bile.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.600
With more and more
phytosterol consumption,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.040
more and more cholesterol is
being flushed out of the body.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.400
Now, even if you eat
a strictly plant-based diet

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.560
without any dietary cholesterol,

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.920
you'd still be getting rid
of more cholesterol

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.560
by eating more phytosterols.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.320
Unfortunately,
like fiber intake,

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.240
plant sterol intake
is way down in modern diets.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.200
We probably evolved

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.360
getting about a thousand
milligrams a day.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.680
But these days
we may only be getting

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.520
about 300 milligrams a day,

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.120
though those eating
more plant foods

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.880
may be getting twice that.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.040
Little bits are found
throughout the plant kingdom

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.680
in vegetables, grains,
legumes, and fruits,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.440
but the highest
whole food sources

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.600
tend to be nuts and seeds.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.120
Phytosterols may help explain

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.840
the cholesterol-lowering effects
of nuts.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.120
But nuts are already a part
of the Portfolio Diet;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.080
why add phytosterols too?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.160
Well, if you look
at the X-axis,

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.040
people may only be getting
a few hundred milligrams a day

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.560
from nuts.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.240
It turns out
there's a continuous

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.080
dose-response relationship

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.920
between phytosterol intake
and LDL cholesterol lowering.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.320
Yeah, going from
very few plant foods

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.040
to lots of plant foods
can draw more cholesterol

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.280
out of the body,
but two grams a day

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.880
can draw out even more,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.520
and that translates
into lower LDL cholesterol

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.480
in the blood.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.720
So, a really healthy
diet's worth

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.600
may drop our LDL
by about six percent,

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.320
but two or three grams a day
can drop our LDL

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:19.680
more like ten percent,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.000
and that alone could reduce
our risk of heart disease

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.160
by about ten percent
over a decade

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.120
or 20% over a lifetime.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.040
That's why we see
heart health guidelines

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.800
recommending
the use of phytosterols

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.120
as a supplementary strategy

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.120
alongside
lifestyle modifications

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.320
to decrease
blood cholesterol levels.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.880
Okay, so phytosterols
are effective,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.800
but are they safe?

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:46.478
I'll address that next.

